-- title:
--   Section off the branch meets only `comp (Sum.inl 0)`
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0$ nonzero and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N_0$, let $\mathfrak P$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ p hpN₀` for level $\Gamma_0(N_0p)$, let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is the ideal generated by $p$, let $\rho_O \colon$ `DRLevel.R p` $\to O$ be a ring map, and let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ with a ring map $\mathrm{to}\kappa \colon O \to \kappa$. Let $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}$ be a resolved package `DRResolvedModelPackageLevel N₀ p 𝔓 O ρO κ toκ`, with total space $Y$, structure morphism $Y \to \operatorname{Spec} O$, comparison morphism $Y \to$ `XO ρO`, and components `comp v`, a family of ideal sheaf data on $Y$ indexed by `X0MqComponents 𝔛reg.width` (two strict transforms `Sum.inl 0`, `Sum.inl 1` and, for each node $n$, a chain `Sum.inr ⟨n, i⟩` with $i$ ranging over `Fin (𝔛reg.width n - 1)`). Let $t \colon \operatorname{Spec} O \to Y$ satisfy $t$ followed by the structure morphism equal to the identity, and assume that the image of the closed point of $O$ under $t$ followed by $Y \to$ `XO ρO` does not lie in the set-theoretic image of `𝔓.comp κ (toκ.comp ρO) 1` followed by the base-change morphism `DRLevel.bcMap ρO toκ` (the canonical map from the fibre over $\kappa$ to the base change over $O$ induced by $\mathrm{to}\kappa$). Then $t$ of the closed point of $O$ lies in the support of `𝔛reg.comp (Sum.inl 0)` and in the support of no other component `𝔛reg.comp w`, $w \neq$ `Sum.inl 0`.
--
--   This is the component-location step for integral sections of the minimal regular model of $X_0(N_0p)$ over a discrete valuation ring with residue characteristic $p$: a section whose reduction avoids the branch of the $p$-fibre singled out by `𝔓.comp … 1` must reduce onto the other strict transform and onto none of the exceptional chains. It is used by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_sections_multidegree_eq_depth_of_exists_schemeHomOver_of_branch`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_sections_multidegree_eq_depth_of_exists_schemeHomOver_of_branch) in the analysis of multidegrees of sections.
